FINAL ANSWER:
**Suggested CODEOWNERS lines.** Nothing was written. Replace `@<troy-github-handle>` with Troy Goode's GitHub username. The tool only has git addresses, and CODEOWNERS needs GitHub handles.

```
/lib/   @<troy-github-handle>
/test/  @<troy-github-handle>   # only if the Troy Goode identity merge is confirmed, see below
```

**Per directory** (surviving lines at HEAD, default `git blame -w -M -C`, bots excluded)

| Path | Top holder | Share | Owner line? |
|---|---|---|---|
| `/lib/` (214 non-blank lines, 1 file sampled) | Troy Goode, merged: 144 lines | 67.3% | Yes. Unmerged: <email redacted> 132 (61.7%) plus troy@laptop.example 12 (5.6%). Holds half either way. |
| `/test/` (820 lines, 7 files) | Troy Goode, merged: 420 lines | 51.2% | Only on the merge. Unmerged, <email redacted> has 388 (47.3%), just under half. |
| Root files (`.`, 323 lines, 6 files) | Douglas Christopher Wilson, 95 lines | 29.4% | No. Nobody holds half. Troy Goode is second at 85 (26.3%). |
| `/.github/` (305 lines, 4 files) | Douglas Christopher Wilson, 92 lines | 30.2% | No. Nobody holds half. Íñigo Marquínez Prado is second at 26.2%. |

The tool did not suggest a root line. It skipped root files because a root pattern would also match every directory. The root row above comes from the `.` block.

**Caveats**

- **Troy Goode identity merge:** the hint rates the link between `<email redacted>` and `troy@laptop.example` as strong, and that is the only reason `/test/` clears 50%. Confirm it before adding the `/test/` line. The `.mailmap` line would be `Troy Goode <<email redacted>>` with `Troy Goode <troy@laptop.example>` as the second address. I did not write it, since you only asked for suggestions.
- **Reformat commit:** `62628c0` ("style: reformat js with 4-space indent and double quotes", Fiona Formatter) was set aside automatically. Without that correction, Troy's merged repo-wide share is 33.3% rather than 39.0%. Both sets of figures are above the 50% line for the directories that get owners.
- **Mechanical rewrites not set aside:** five candidates were kept in the counts. One is by Troy Goode (`fcd2b56`, 11 surviving lines). The rest are by Douglas Christopher Wilson (`739dc11`, `00d6eec`, `344ce1e`, `9c2b59d`, 28 lines together). The check was partial: it examined 136 commits holding surviving lines.
- **Excluded:** `dependabot[bot]` (10 lines, 11 commits). Copy detection is the default `-C`. No placeholder identities appeared.
- **Owners are not reviewers:** surviving lines show who wrote the code that is left, not who should review changes to it.

