FINAL ANSWER:
Suggested CODEOWNERS lines (blame on HEAD, bots excluded, formatting commit `62628c0` re-attributed to pre-reformat authors):

```
/lib/   @troygoode   # 150 of 238 lines (63%)
/test/  @troygoode   # 486 of 966 lines (50.3%)
```

- **`lib/`**: Troy Goode holds 63%. Owner.
- **`test/`**: Troy Goode holds 50.3%, which meets the "at least half" bar but by only 3 lines. Treat it as borderline; a few more lines from someone else would drop Troy below half.
- **`.github/`**: no majority owner. Top is Douglas Christopher Wilson at 29.5% (108 of 366), then Íñigo Marquínez Prado at 25.7%. No line.
- **Root files** (README.md, HISTORY.md, package.json, LICENSE, .gitignore, .eslintrc.yml, as one group): no majority owner. Top is Troy Goode at 29.4%, then Douglas at 27.7%. No line.

Caveats:
- **Douglas Christopher Wilson is excluded** even though he is the #2 test owner (41.5%) and the top `.github/` owner. His last commit is 2021-09-07, while the repo's newest commit is 2026-04-12, so naming him would route reviews to someone inactive.
- **`@troygoode` is my inference** from the git email `<email redacted>`. Confirm the GitHub login before committing the file.
- **Re-attribution is a heuristic.** The reformat commit changed quotes as well as whitespace, so `git blame --ignore-rev` alone left 237 lib/test lines on it. I matched those lines to their parent-commit versions by normalized content. Every such line found a match, but the 3-line margin on `test/` is only as good as that match.
- **I did not run the skill's `scripts/ownership.mjs`.** It uses a 0.70 coverage threshold and a 0.25 orphan threshold, which don't match your half-of-surviving-lines rule. Nothing was written to the repo.
- **Not produced:** the per-zone risk report and the orphaned/bus-factor-1 split. Only the ownership shares were asked for.
